I'm not a Slash'EM player (yet), but I do have one thought:

2013-01-31 23:21 – Prometheus77:
> Since there has been a number of posts on here recently from SLASH'EM
players, I wanted to informally poll the community again on opinions of
role difficulty. AFAIK, there's no online SLASH'EM community comparable
to NAO that tracks deaths and has enough of a sample of ascensions to
rate by observed ascension probability. Therefore, I just updated
Nethackwiki with my own subjective ordering after several months and
several ascensions, and would like to solicit others' opinions on where
they agree/disagree with these rankings.
>
> Here's what I got, from easiest to hardest:
> Role/Notes
> Knight - Start with plate mail, long sword, Str 18/**
> Monk - Powerful techniques and automatic AC bonuses as level increases
> Valkyrie - Start with spear instead of long sword, Mjollnir much more
powerful
> Samurai
> Yeoman - Two powerful guaranteed sacrifice gifts: Sword of Justice and
Reaper
> Barbarian
> Rogue - Ultra-powerful guaranteed sacrifice gift: Bat from Hell
> Caveman - Gets underground vision but the Sceptre of Might is
considerably weaker
> Wizard
> Undead Slayer - Slow, weak fighter whose main advantages (drain
resistance and immunity to sickness) don't matter until late in the game
Don't say that.  I've been playing with the convict patch for a time
(designed to be harder than tourist), and that role's sickness
resistance is what (mostly, at least) keeps him from starving early on.
 He just feasts on all those zombie and mummy corpses…

> Ranger - Bows require two hands to wield in SLASH'EM
> Flame Mage - Starts with a hell hound pup and a wand of fire but
otherwise far weaker than Wizard
> Priest
> Ice Mage - Starts with a winter wolf but weaker than either Wizard or
Flame Mage
> Necromancer - First sacrifice gift Serpent's Tongue moderately good,
otherwise like Undead Slayer with drain resistance and immunity only
mattering late in game
> Archaeologist - Fedora acts as luckstone
> Healer 	
> Tourist

